# =============================================================================
# Integration test config — copy to .env.test (or set in your shell) and fill in.
# =============================================================================
#
# HARD REQUIREMENT (post data-incident, 2026-05): integration tests MUST run
# against a SEPARATE Supabase test project, not prod. The test runner refuses
# to start if any of these vars equal their prod counterparts in .env:
#
#   VITE_SUPABASE_TEST_URL          must NOT equal VITE_SUPABASE_URL
#   SUPABASE_TEST_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY  must NOT equal SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
#
# How to spin up a test project:
# - Option A: create a free-tier Supabase project at https://supabase.com,
#   apply this repo's migrations to it (`supabase db push --linked`), and
#   paste its URL + service-role key below.
# - Option B (local stack — requires Docker, which is NOT running on
#   Andrew's machine):
#     supabase start
#     VITE_SUPABASE_TEST_URL=http://localhost:54321
#     SUPABASE_TEST_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=<service role from `supabase status`>
#
# Cleanup contract: every integration test MUST restore mutated rows in
# afterAll OR (preferred) create temp orgs/workspaces in the test and drop
# them on cleanup. Never mutate rows that existed before the test ran.
# =============================================================================

# Required. Must be a separate Supabase project — NOT prod.
VITE_SUPABASE_TEST_URL=https://YOUR-TEST-PROJECT.supabase.co

# Required. Service-role key from the test project dashboard. Do NOT paste the
# anon/publishable key — service role is needed to bypass RLS for seeding.
SUPABASE_TEST_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-test-service-role-key

# Required for the RLS regression test (src/test/rls-regression.test.ts). This
# is the publishable/anon key from the SAME test project. Used by the test to
# sign in test users via signInWithPassword.
VITE_SUPABASE_TEST_ANON_KEY=your-test-anon-key

# Required. Explicit opt-in flag. Without this set to "true", vitest excludes
# every *.integration.test.ts file from the run — so a stray `npm test`
# invocation cannot accidentally execute against any live DB.
VITEST_INTEGRATION_OK=true
